  "notes": "Source: Apex College of Veterinary Technology Catalog and Handbook 1/1/25 Volume 10.0 (https://www.apexcvt.edu/_files/ugd/5484e0_80d8910a900040d1b3096d592abdebd7.pdf), 'Degree Program - associate in applied science - Veterinary Technology (115.75 quarter credits)'. The catalog states 'The Veterinary Technology program has curriculum divided into eight fulltime quarters in standard progression.' Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the quarter listings (Quarter 1-8) and the course-description pages (pp. 19-28). All credits are QUARTER credits as printed. Each quarter's course sum reconciles with the catalog's printed quarter total, and the eight quarter totals sum to the printed program total of 115.75 quarter credits. Courses marked 'General Education' in the catalog are category 'core' with the catalog's area label in core_area; all others are 'major'. 'Admission into the Veterinary Technology program' is the catalog's only prerequisite for Quarter 1 courses, VET 204, and VET 205; it is an admission condition, not a course, so it is documented here rather than carried as a machine prereq. Two prerequisite annotations in the catalog do not match the curriculum as printed: (1) VET 702 lists 'VET 503 - Exotic and Laboratory Animal Nursing' but no VET 503 exists anywhere in the catalog - the only Exotic and Laboratory Animal Nursing course is VET 406 (Quarter 4), recorded as VET 406; (2) VET 801 lists 'VET 703 - Large Animal Nursing' but VET 703 is 'Survey of Companion Animal Diseases' per the course listing (VET 305 is Large Animal Nursing); the code is recorded as printed (VET 703). The course-description section also describes 'VET 105 - Greek, Latin, and Veterinary Culture' (3.0 credits), which appears in NO quarter listing; the eight quarter sums reconcile to the printed 115.75 total without it, so it is excluded and documented here. transfer_confidence is 'advisory': AAS workforce program; the catalog publishes no TCCNS or articulation equivalencies, so tccns mirrors the local course code.",
